.TH TULPAR-FILES 1 "2026" "tulpar 0.6.0" "Tulpar Manual"
.SH NAME
tulpar-files \- list the files of an installed package
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tulpar files
.RI [ options "] " name
.br
.B tulpar f
.RI [ options "] " name
.br
.B tulpar \-f
.RI [ options "] " name
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints the absolute path of every file recorded for the installed
package
.IR name ,
one per line.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dest " " \fIpath\fR
Operate on the database of an alternate root.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Print the package name, version and file list as a JSON object instead of human-readable text. See
.BR tulpar-json (7).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if the package is not installed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tulpar (1),
.BR tulpar-owns (1),
.BR tulpar-verify (1),
.BR tulpar-json (7)
